200eff92 [deepseek-v4] #The protocol you're thinking of is called NTP (Network Time Protocol). A simpler version
200eff92 [deepseek-v4] #used in many embedded devices is SNTP (Simple Network Time Protocol), which is a subset of
200eff93 [deepseek-v4] #NTP.
200eff93 [deepseek-v4] #
200eff93 [deepseek-v4] #Both use a compact binary packet (typically 48 or 64 bytes) with 64‑bit timestamps and a round‑trip
200eff93 [deepseek-v4] #measurement mechanism. That's the “internet time protocol” pattern you described.
