201156e4 [deepseek-v4] #Yes, using Unix epoch seconds (or milliseconds) as the parameter for `setClock` is a natural choice
201156e5 [deepseek-v4] #– it's universally recognised and easy to handle on both the host and the Pico.
201156e5 [deepseek-v4] #
201156e5 [deepseek-v4] #If you want sub‑second precision, milliseconds (13‑digit int) work well; otherwise seconds
201156e5 [deepseek-v4] #(10‑digit) suffice for most cases. The Pico’s `rtc_set_datetime` expects a `datetime_t` struct, so
201156e6 [deepseek-v4] #you’ll convert the epoch to year/month/day/hour/minute/second on the device side. That’s
