20130346 [nitro@ryzen5] does pico sdk have a performance counter
201303c2 [deepseek-v4] # ꔀ nitrologic Relay 1.8.8 ⛲  deepseek-v4 🐋 🪠 0.7° $0.000 504B 7.24s
201303c2 [deepseek-v4] #Yes, the Raspberry Pi Pico SDK includes support for performance counters, primarily through the
201303c2 [deepseek-v4] #Data Watchpoint and Trace (DWT) unit's cycle counter on the RP2040 microcontroller.
201303c2 [deepseek-v4] #
201303c3 [deepseek-v4] #The SDK provides a dedicated library called `pico_perf_counter` which wraps the DWT cycle
201303c3 [deepseek-v4] #counter and offers functions for measuring CPU cycles with high accuracy. You can enable it by
201303c3 [deepseek-v4] #adding `pico_perf_counter` to your CMake target's `target_link_libraries`. Basic usage:
201303c3 [deepseek-v4] #
201303c4 [deepseek-v4] #- `perf_counter_init()` — initializes the DWT counter.
201303c4 [deepseek-v4] #- `perf_counter_begin()` / `perf_counter_end()` — marks the start/end of a measurement interval.
201303c4 [deepseek-v4] #- `perf_counter_get_count()` — returns the elapsed cycles since initialization.
201303c4 [deepseek-v4] #- `perf_counter_get_elapsed()` — returns cycles between the last begin and end calls.
201303c5 [deepseek-v4] #
201303c5 [deepseek-v4] #Alternatively, you can directly access the DWT cycle counter via `hardware_dwt`. The relevant
201303c5 [deepseek-v4] #functions (available when `<hardware/dwt.h>` is included) include:
201303c5 [deepseek-v4] #
201303c6 [deepseek-v4] #- `dwt_init()` — enables the cycle counter.
201303c6 [deepseek-v4] #- `dwt_get_cycle_count()` — reads the current cycle count.
201303c6 [deepseek-v4] #- `dwt_reset_cycle_count()` — resets the counter to zero.
201303c6 [deepseek-v4] #
201303c7 [deepseek-v4] #Both approaches provide cycle‑accurate timing for performance analysis, benchmarking, and
201303c7 [deepseek-v4] #profiling.
201303c7 [deepseek-v4] #
201303c7 [deepseek-v4] #If you need a higher‑resolution counter beyond the 48 MHz system clock (e.g., for sub‑cycle
201303c8 [deepseek-v4] #measurements), that is not available on the RP2040, but the DWT cycle counter is sufficient for
201303c8 [deepseek-v4] #most performance‑sensitive code.
201303c8 [deepseek-v4] #
