20b37014 [kimi-k2.7-code] # ꔀ nitrologic Relay 1.8.8 ⛲  kimi-k2.7-code 🜁 🪠 🧊 $0.003 8.390KB 6.40s
20b37015 [kimi-k2.7-code] #The RP2350 has 2 PIO blocks, the same as the RP2040.
20b37015 [kimi-k2.7-code] #
20b37015 [kimi-k2.7-code] #Each PIO block has 4 state machines, giving you 8 state machines total.
20b37015 [kimi-k2.7-code] #
20b37016 [kimi-k2.7-code] #Each block also has:
20b37016 [kimi-k2.7-code] #- 32 instruction slots
20b37016 [kimi-k2.7-code] #- 4 × 32-bit shift registers
20b37016 [kimi-k2.7-code] #- TX/RX FIFOs per state machine
20b37017 [kimi-k2.7-code] #- Flexible GPIO mapping
20b37017 [kimi-k2.7-code] #
20b37017 [kimi-k2.7-code] #The RP2350 PIO is backwards-compatible with the RP2040 but adds a few new instructions and
20b37017 [kimi-k2.7-code] #features. For your VGA project, this is plenty — you could dedicate one or two PIO state machines
20b37018 [kimi-k2.7-code] #to generate the pixel clock, H-sync, and V-sync, while the CPU or DMA feeds pixel data into the
20b37018 [kimi-k2.7-code] #FIFO.
20b37018 [kimi-k2.7-code] #
20b37018 [kimi-k2.7-code] #Do you want a sketch of how to use PIO for VGA timing on the RP2350?
20b37018 [kimi-k2.7-code] #
