213610a0 [grok-build-0.1] # ꔀ nitrologic Relay 1.8.8 ⛲  grok-build-0.1 𝕏 🪣 0.7° $0.053 220.7KB 16.87s
213610a1 [grok-build-0.1] #• Got the full relay source + supporting files.* Thanks for the drop.
213610a1 [grok-build-0.1] #
213610a1 [grok-build-0.1] #Focusing on the new star system for shares as you mentioned.
213610a2 [grok-build-0.1] #
213610a2 [grok-build-0.1] #Current star logic (as implemented)
213610a2 [grok-build-0.1] #
213610a2 [grok-build-0.1] #From the code:
213610a3 [grok-build-0.1] #
213610a3 [grok-build-0.1] #- Shares can have a `.stars` string (e.g. `""`, `"★"`, etc.).
213610a3 [grok-build-0.1] #- In `listShare(true)` (the sorted-by-size path used by star command), it displays:
213610a3 [grok-build-0.1] #
213610a4 [grok-build-0.1] #  const stars = share.stars || "-";
213610a4 [grok-build-0.1] #
213610a4 [grok-build-0.1] #- `starCommand`:
213610a4 [grok-build-0.1] #  - `star` (no args) → calls `listShare(true)` and sets `listCommand = "star"`
213610a5 [grok-build-0.1] #  - `star <index>` → clears stars on that share
213610a5 [grok-build-0.1] #  - `star <index> <chars>` → appends the chars to existing stars
213610a5 [grok-build-0.1] #- In `commitShares` (the critical path):
213610a5 [grok-build-0.1] #
213610a6 [grok-build-0.1] #  const stars = share.stars || "";
213610a6 [grok-build-0.1] #  if (roha.config.starshare && (stars.length === 0)) isShared = false;
213610a6 [grok-build-0.1] #
213610a6 [grok-build-0.1] #- `starshare` config flag (default false) is documented as: "conserve file share by star"
213610a7 [grok-build-0.1] #
213610a7 [grok-build-0.1] #So the intended model appears to be:
213610a7 [grok-build-0.1] #- When `starshare` is on, only shares that have a non-empty `.stars` value get committed into the
213610a7 [grok-build-0.1] #context.
213610a8 [grok-build-0.1] #- Stars are basically a lightweight include/exclude + priority tag.
213610a8 [grok-build-0.1] #
213610a8 [grok-build-0.1] #Observations / potential debug points
213610a8 [grok-build-0.1] #
213610a9 [grok-build-0.1] #1. Star accumulation vs. set semantics
213610a9 [grok-build-0.1] #   The current append behavior (`stars = (share.stars || "") + addStars`) means repeated `star 3
213610a9 [grok-build-0.1] #` would give `""`. Is that desired, or should it be a set/replace?
213610a9 [grok-build-0.1] #
213610aa [grok-build-0.1] #2. Clearing logic
213610aa [grok-build-0.1] #   `star <index>` with no second token sets `share.stars = ""`.
213610aa [grok-build-0.1] #   This is then treated as "no stars" in both display and `commitShares`. Seems intentional, but
213610aa [grok-build-0.1] #the display falls back to `"-"` only at list time.
213610ab [grok-build-0.1] #
213610ab [grok-build-0.1] #3. shareList dependency
213610ab [grok-build-0.1] #   `starCommand` only works with numeric indices when `shareList` was populated by the last
213610ab [grok-build-0.1] #`listShare(true)`.
213610ac [grok-build-0.1] #   If someone does `/star 2` without first doing a bare `/star`, `shareList` may be stale or empty.
213610ac [grok-build-0.1] #
213610ac [grok-build-0.1] #4. Persistence & keyed shares
213610ac [grok-build-0.1] #   Stars live on the `Share` objects inside `roha.sharedFiles` → `roha.keyedShares[project]`.
213610ad [grok-build-0.1] #   They should survive `/push` and project switches, but I don't see any migration or sanitization
213610ad [grok-build-0.1] #if old shares lack the `stars` field.
213610ad [grok-build-0.1] #
213610ad [grok-build-0.1] #5. commitShares interaction with other filters
213610ae [grok-build-0.1] #   The star check happens after the `tag` filter and size check.
213610ae [grok-build-0.1] #   When `starshare` is true, even a tagged share with no stars gets dropped.
213610ae [grok-build-0.1] #
213610ae [grok-build-0.1] #6. Display in listShare
213610af [grok-build-0.1] #   When not sorting (the other `listShare(false)` path), stars are still shown, but the command
213610af [grok-build-0.1] #only triggers the sorted version.
213610af [grok-build-0.1] #
213610af [grok-build-0.1] #7. No star count / weighting yet
213610b0 [grok-build-0.1] #   Currently stars are just truthy length. No distinction between one star vs. three yet.
213610b0 [grok-build-0.1] #
213610b0 [grok-build-0.1] #Questions to help debug
213610b0 [grok-build-0.1] #
213610b1 [grok-build-0.1] #- What specific symptom are you seeing right now?
213610b1 [grok-build-0.1] #  - Stars not being respected on commit?
213610b1 [grok-build-0.1] #  - Stars not persisting across `/push` or project load?
213610b1 [grok-build-0.1] #  - Index selection not matching the list?
213610b2 [grok-build-0.1] #  - Stars being cleared unexpectedly?
213610b2 [grok-build-0.1] #  - Something else?
213610b2 [grok-build-0.1] #
213610b2 [grok-build-0.1] #- Are you aiming for:
213610b3 [grok-build-0.1] #  - Simple include/exclude (star = keep, no star = drop when flag on)
213610b3 [grok-build-0.1] #  - Priority weighting (more stars = higher priority / earlier in context)
213610b3 [grok-build-0.1] #  - Named star types (e.g. `` = core, `*` = optional)
213610b3 [grok-build-0.1] #
213610b4 [grok-build-0.1] #- Do you want stars to be visible in the regular `/share` list or only when explicitly in star
213610b4 [grok-build-0.1] #mode?
213610b4 [grok-build-0.1] #
213610b4 [grok-build-0.1] #Let me know the exact failure mode or the desired behavior and I'll walk through the relevant
213610b4 [grok-build-0.1] #functions with you (without dumping code unless you ask for a specific fix).
213610b5 [grok-build-0.1] #
