2136179e [grok-build-0.1] #
2136179f [grok-build-0.1] #
2136179f [grok-build-0.1] #What's happening
2136179f [grok-build-0.1] #
2136179f [grok-build-0.1] #1. When `starshare` is `true` and a share has no stars, it forces `isShared = false`.
213617a0 [grok-build-0.1] #2. The condition `modified || !isShared` then becomes `true` in almost every case.
213617a0 [grok-build-0.1] #3. So it calls `shareBlob` anyway and adds the path to `rohaSharePaths`.
213617a0 [grok-build-0.1] #4. Result: all shares get included regardless of stars.
213617a0 [grok-build-0.1] #
213617a1 [grok-build-0.1] #The star check is being used to force sharing instead of prevent it.
213617a1 [grok-build-0.1] #
213617a1 [grok-build-0.1] #Correct intent (based on your config description)
213617a1 [grok-build-0.1] #
213617a2 [grok-build-0.1] #When `starshare` is true:
213617a2 [grok-build-0.1] #- Only shares that have a non-empty `stars` value should have their content committed.
