21365ad0 [grok-build-0.1] # ꔀ nitrologic Relay 1.8.8 ⛲  grok-build-0.1 𝕏 🪠 0.7° $0.054 234.0KB 10.14s
21365ad0 [grok-build-0.1] #• Discussion on the starshare behaviour*
21365ad0 [grok-build-0.1] #
21365ad1 [grok-build-0.1] #The core issue seems to be a mismatch between what the flag is intended to do and what actually
21365ad1 [grok-build-0.1] #happens at commit time.
21365ad1 [grok-build-0.1] #
21365ad1 [grok-build-0.1] #Intended behaviour (from the flag name and config description)
21365ad2 [grok-build-0.1] #When `starshare` is enabled, the system should be more selective: only shares that have been
21365ad2 [grok-build-0.1] #explicitly marked with stars should have their content loaded into the model context. Unstarred
21365ad2 [grok-build-0.1] #shares should remain in the share list (for visibility and management) but be excluded from the
21365ad2 [grok-build-0.1] #actual payload on `/commit` or `/push`.
21365ad3 [grok-build-0.1] #
21365ad3 [grok-build-0.1] #This is a "conserve tokens" or "explicit opt-in" mechanism.
21365ad3 [grok-build-0.1] #
21365ad3 [grok-build-0.1] #Current flow problems
21365ad4 [grok-build-0.1] #The tracking of "has this share already been committed?" (`rohaSharePaths`) is being mixed with the
21365ad4 [grok-build-0.1] #star decision. Once a share has been seen before, the logic treats it as already "shared", which
21365ad4 [grok-build-0.1] #then overrides the star check in some paths.
21365ad4 [grok-build-0.1] #
21365ad5 [grok-build-0.1] #When a share has no stars, the code is forcing a state that still causes the content to be sent
21365ad5 [grok-build-0.1] #(often because it looks like it needs a refresh or hasn't been marked as shared yet). This makes
21365ad5 [grok-build-0.1] #the star filter ineffective.
21365ad5 [grok-build-0.1] #
21365ad6 [grok-build-0.1] #Key areas worth discussing
21365ad6 [grok-build-0.1] #
21365ad6 [grok-build-0.1] #• 1. When should the star filter be evaluated?*
21365ad6 [grok-build-0.1] #- Only at the moment of commit (so the list can still show everything for management)?
21365ad7 [grok-build-0.1] #- Or should unstarred shares be prevented from entering `rohaSharePaths` at all when `starshare` is
21365ad7 [grok-build-0.1] #on?
21365ad7 [grok-build-0.1] #- Should starring a share after it has already been committed trigger an immediate re-commit, or
21365ad7 [grok-build-0.1] #only on the next explicit `/push`?
21365ad8 [grok-build-0.1] #
21365ad8 [grok-build-0.1] #• 2. Separation of concerns*
21365ad8 [grok-build-0.1] #Right now there appear to be several overlapping lists:
21365ad8 [grok-build-0.1] #- The persistent share metadata (`roha.sharedFiles` / keyed shares)
21365ad9 [grok-build-0.1] #- The "currently in context" list (`rohaSharePaths`)
21365ad9 [grok-build-0.1] #- The visual list used for commands like `star`
21365ad9 [grok-build-0.1] #
21365ad9 [grok-build-0.1] #It might be cleaner to treat "should this share participate in the current context?" as a derived
21365ada [grok-build-0.1] #decision at commit time, rather than mutating the "already shared" tracking based on stars.
21365ada [grok-build-0.1] #
21365ada [grok-build-0.1] #• 3. Handling of "modified" shares*
21365ada [grok-build-0.1] #The existing logic has a strong bias toward re-sending anything that has changed or isn't yet in
21365adb [grok-build-0.1] #the active path list. When `starshare` is active, this bias needs to be subordinated to the star
21365adb [grok-build-0.1] #check. A share that is modified but unstarred should probably stay out, even if it looks "dirty".
21365adb [grok-build-0.1] #
21365adb [grok-build-0.1] #• 4. What does "no stars" actually mean?*
21365adc [grok-build-0.1] #- Is an empty star field the same as "never evaluated"?
21365adc [grok-build-0.1] #- Should there be an explicit "exclude" state, or is absence of stars sufficient?
21365adc [grok-build-0.1] #- Do you want stars to be additive (more stars = higher priority) or just a binary "included / not
21365adc [grok-build-0.1] #included" marker?
21365add [grok-build-0.1] #
21365add [grok-build-0.1] #• 5. User workflow implications*
21365add [grok-build-0.1] #- Should `/share` and `/list` (or the star list) behave differently when `starshare` is true?
21365add [grok-build-0.1] #- Should there be a visible indicator in the normal share listing that some shares are currently
21365ade [grok-build-0.1] #filtered out due to stars?
21365ade [grok-build-0.1] #- What happens on project load or `/reset`? Should star status survive, or should the flag only
21365ade [grok-build-0.1] #affect the current session's commit decisions?
21365ade [grok-build-0.1] #
21365adf [grok-build-0.1] #• 6. Simpler mental model*
21365adf [grok-build-0.1] #One possible direction is to make the star check the first gate at commit time:
21365adf [grok-build-0.1] #- If `starshare` is on, only consider shares that have a non-empty stars value.
21365ae0 [grok-build-0.1] #- The "has this been sent before" and "has it changed" logic only applies inside that filtered set.
21365ae0 [grok-build-0.1] #
21365ae0 [grok-build-0.1] #This would keep the management list complete while making the context payload respect the flag.
21365ae0 [grok-build-0.1] #
21365ae1 [grok-build-0.1] #Would you like to talk through any of these points in more detail? For example:
21365ae1 [grok-build-0.1] #- How you expect a newly shared file to behave if it has no stars yet
21365ae1 [grok-build-0.1] #- Whether you want the filter to be "strict" (never send unstarred) or "advisory"
21365ae1 [grok-build-0.1] #- How starring/unstarring should interact with an already-active conversation
21365ae2 [grok-build-0.1] #
21365ae2 [grok-build-0.1] #Happy to explore the trade-offs without jumping to implementation details.
21365ae2 [grok-build-0.1] #
