2136bf22 [grok-build-0.1] #It's a substantial Deno-based relay / multi-LLM client with a lot of personality. From a quick pass
2136bf22 [grok-build-0.1] #I can see it does:
2136bf23 [grok-build-0.1] #
2136bf23 [grok-build-0.1] #- Unified interface across OpenAI, Anthropic, Google Gemini, DeepSeek (and others)
2136bf23 [grok-build-0.1] #- File sharing / vision / tool calling with a custom "forge" persistence layer
2136bf23 [grok-build-0.1] #- History management with squashing, sessions, and project-aware sharing
2136bf23 [grok-build-0.1] #- Custom prompt system (`slopprompt`), ANSI rendering, tables, and some fun Unicode handling
2136bf23 [grok-build-0.1] #- TTS support (Gemini + OpenAI)
2136bf24 [grok-build-0.1] #- Quite a few configuration flags and a "slop" worker system
2136bf24 [grok-build-0.1] #
2136bf24 [grok-build-0.1] #Initial observations
2136bf24 [grok-build-0.1] #
2136bf25 [grok-build-0.1] #• Strengths*
2136bf25 [grok-build-0.1] #- Very pragmatic. You clearly ship a lot of real usage through this.
2136bf25 [grok-build-0.1] #- Good provider abstraction (the endpoint objects are clean).
2136bf25 [grok-build-0.1] #- Thoughtful about cost tracking, caching, and "cold" models.
2136bf26 [grok-build-0.1] #- The `plainHistory` / `strictHistory` / `multiHistory` split is interesting.
2136bf26 [grok-build-0.1] #
2136bf26 [grok-build-0.1] #• Areas that stand out (in no particular order)*
2136bf26 [grok-build-0.1] #
2136bf27 [grok-build-0.1] #1. File size & structure
2136bf27 [grok-build-0.1] #   135k lines in one file is getting painful. The `relay()` function + all the history
2136bf27 [grok-build-0.1] #transformation logic + provider adapters are doing a lot.
2136bf27 [grok-build-0.1] #
2136bf27 [grok-build-0.1] #2. History transformations
2136bf28 [grok-build-0.1] #   You have several different ways of turning `rohaHistory` into a provider payload
2136bf28 [grok-build-0.1] #(`plainHistory`, `strictHistory`, `multiHistory`, `inlineHistory`). This is fragile and easy to get
2136bf28 [grok-build-0.1] #out of sync when adding new roles or fields.
2136bf29 [grok-build-0.1] #
2136bf29 [grok-build-0.1] #3. State management
2136bf29 [grok-build-0.1] #   Global `roha`, `rohaHistory`, `rohaEndpoint`, etc. + the `Plop` class. It works, but it makes
2136bf29 [grok-build-0.1] #testing and reasoning about concurrent sessions harder (you even have a comment acknowledging
2136bf2a [grok-build-0.1] #this).
2136bf2a [grok-build-0.1] #
2136bf2a [grok-build-0.1] #4. Provider-specific logic
2136bf2a [grok-build-0.1] #   Some of the Gemini and Anthropic handling has quite a bit of special-case code. The tool call
2136bf2a [grok-build-0.1] #translation layers are also spread out.
2136bf2b [grok-build-0.1] #
2136bf2b [grok-build-0.1] #5. Error handling & recovery
2136bf2b [grok-build-0.1] #   Lots of places catch and `echo`, but the actual failure modes (especially around tool calls and
2136bf2b [grok-build-0.1] #long contexts) are still fairly loud.
2136bf2b [grok-build-0.1] #
