2140bb31 [grok-build-0.1] #• Thank you for sharing the vidbit project files.*
2140bb31 [grok-build-0.1] #
2140bb31 [grok-build-0.1] #I've received the complete set of sources (colorbit, fs, i2s, json, monobit, nitro,
2140bb31 [grok-build-0.1] #pal288p/pal576i, ps2, shapes, spkr, vidbit, vidbit2350, and the associated headers). This is a
2140bb32 [grok-build-0.1] #substantial RP2350-based PAL video generator using PIO for precise signal timing, DMA for frame
2140bb32 [grok-build-0.1] #delivery, PDM-style color, C64-style bitmap text, PS/2 input, basic audio, and a littlefs-backed
2140bb32 [grok-build-0.1] #filesystem.
2140bb32 [grok-build-0.1] #
2140bb32 [grok-build-0.1] #Quick observations (high level)
2140bb32 [grok-build-0.1] #- The core video work is split between progressive (288p) and interlaced (576i) paths.
2140bb32 [grok-build-0.1] #- `vidbit2350.cpp` is the main application entry point.
2140bb32 [grok-build-0.1] #- Color handling has both a "color train" mode and a more complex pump/fifo approach.
2140bb33 [grok-build-0.1] #- Text rendering uses a compact 8×8 font with bit-flipping helpers.
2140bb33 [grok-build-0.1] #- There's a lot of experimental / commented code (WST teletext, chroma, active-line sync, etc.).
2140bb33 [grok-build-0.1] #- JSON and RPC scaffolding exists for host communication.
2140bb33 [grok-build-0.1] #
2140bb33 [grok-build-0.1] #If the files are intended as new or updated content, please let me know what has changed or what
2140bb33 [grok-build-0.1] #you'd like me to focus on.
2140bb33 [grok-build-0.1] #
2140bb33 [grok-build-0.1] #How would you like to proceed?
2140bb33 [grok-build-0.1] #- Review a specific module or function for issues?
2140bb34 [grok-build-0.1] #- Help debug timing, DMA, or PIO configuration?
2140bb34 [grok-build-0.1] #- Refactor or clean up a particular area?
2140bb34 [grok-build-0.1] #- Add or extend a feature (e.g. better color, more efficient text, audio improvements)?
2140bb34 [grok-build-0.1] #- Something else?
2140bb35 [grok-build-0.1] #
