2140c365 [grok-build-0.1] # ꔀ nitrologic Relay 1.9.0 ⛲  grok-build-0.1 𝕏 🪠 0.7° $0.080 179.2KB 11.70s
2140c365 [grok-build-0.1] #• Thanks for sharing the files.* This looks like a substantial RP2350 PAL video generator
2140c365 [grok-build-0.1] #project ("vidbit") with PIO-driven signal generation, multiple rendering modes, audio, input, and a
2140c365 [grok-build-0.1] #JSON-RPC control layer.
2140c366 [grok-build-0.1] #
2140c366 [grok-build-0.1] #Quick observations (no assumptions on intent)
2140c366 [grok-build-0.1] #
2140c366 [grok-build-0.1] #- The project supports both progressive (288p) and interlaced (576i) PAL output with tight
2140c366 [grok-build-0.1] #cycle-accurate timing.
2140c367 [grok-build-0.1] #- There are two parallel drawing systems (`monobit.cpp` vs `pal576i.cpp` / `pal288p.cpp`) — one for
2140c367 [grok-build-0.1] #1-bit and one for 2-bit per pixel.
2140c367 [grok-build-0.1] #- Color generation uses PDM patterns (`colorbit.cpp`) with separate "color train" and "color pump"
2140c367 [grok-build-0.1] #approaches under `#ifdef COLORTRAIN` / `#ifdef COLOR`.
2140c367 [grok-build-0.1] #- Heavy conditional compilation (`#ifdef LACE`, `COLOR`, `GREY`, `WST`, `CHROMA`, `HAS_ACTIVE`,
2140c368 [grok-build-0.1] #etc.) to support different hardware configurations.
2140c368 [grok-build-0.1] #- Teletext (WST) support is present but appears incomplete in the current paste (`receiveBuffer()`
2140c368 [grok-build-0.1] #is empty).
2140c368 [grok-build-0.1] #- Audio path has both I2S and a simple speaker PIO, plus some noise generation.
2140c369 [grok-build-0.1] #- There's an RPC/JSON control surface over CDC + an event sink system.
2140c369 [grok-build-0.1] #
2140c369 [grok-build-0.1] #Areas that stand out as potentially needing attention
2140c369 [grok-build-0.1] #
2140c369 [grok-build-0.1] #1. Duplicated drawing primitives — `plot`/`rect`/`text` families exist in multiple files
2140c36a [grok-build-0.1] #with slight variations (1-bit vs 2-bit, even/odd fields). This makes maintenance error-prone.
2140c36a [grok-build-0.1] #2. Empty / stub functions — `receiveBuffer()` in `pal576i.cpp` and some banner handling.
2140c36a [grok-build-0.1] #3. Timing constants are scattered and some are duplicated (e.g. sync pulse values in both
2140c36a [grok-build-0.1] #`pal576i.cpp` and `pal288p.cpp`).
2140c36a [grok-build-0.1] #4. DMA + PIO interaction — The active line / video DMA handoff and stall detection logic is
2140c36a [grok-build-0.1] #quite intricate. Easy to introduce subtle desyncs when changing modes.
2140c36a [grok-build-0.1] #5. C64 font rendering — Uses a 64-bit font table with bit-flipping helpers. The 2-bit path
2140c36a [grok-build-0.1] #uses `flipBits2[]` which is precomputed, but the 1-bit path recomputes on the fly in some places.
2140c36b [grok-build-0.1] #
2140c36b [grok-build-0.1] #Would you like me to:
2140c36b [grok-build-0.1] #
2140c36b [grok-build-0.1] #- Review a specific file or subsystem in detail (e.g. the color PDM logic, DMA setup, or the
2140c36b [grok-build-0.1] #interlaced drawing path)?
2140c36b [grok-build-0.1] #- Help consolidate the duplicated drawing code?
2140c36c [grok-build-0.1] #- Look for potential bugs in the video field/DMA sequencing?
2140c36c [grok-build-0.1] #- Something else?
2140c36c [grok-build-0.1] #
2140c36c [grok-build-0.1] #Just let me know what you're trying to achieve or which part you'd like feedback on.
2140c36d [grok-build-0.1] #
2140c36d [roha] [RELAY] commitShares starCount 0
