2148069e [grok-build-0.1] #- A broadcast mechanism that pushes messages out from the relay to connected bots.
2148069e [grok-build-0.1] #- The bots appear to be reacting to the same events/triggers, resulting in unison behavior.
2148069e [grok-build-0.1] #
2148069f [grok-build-0.1] #This is a classic hub + multiple clients pattern, but right now it sounds like the hub is
2148069f [grok-build-0.1] #treating all connected bots as equivalent listeners rather than distinct agents.
2148069f [grok-build-0.1] #
214806a0 [grok-build-0.1] #Key architectural questions we should resolve
214806a0 [grok-build-0.1] #
214806a0 [grok-build-0.1] #1. Routing vs Broadcasting
214806a0 [grok-build-0.1] #   - Currently it seems like most messages are being broadcast to all bots.
214806a1 [grok-build-0.1] #   - Do you want the relay to act as a smart router (deciding which bot(s) should receive a
214806a1 [grok-build-0.1] #message), or should it stay as a dumb message bus where the bots themselves decide whether to act?
214806a1 [grok-build-0.1] #
214806a1 [grok-build-0.1] #2. Bot Identity & Addressing
214806a2 [grok-build-0.1] #   - How should users (or the system) target a specific bot?
214806a2 [grok-build-0.1] #     - Discord @mentions?
214806a2 [grok-build-0.1] #     - Prefixes in the message?
214806a2 [grok-build-0.1] #     - Dedicated channels per bot?
214806a3 [grok-build-0.1] #     - Bot-specific commands?
214806a3 [grok-build-0.1] #   - Should the bots be able to address each other directly?
214806a3 [grok-build-0.1] #
214806a3 [grok-build-0.1] #3. Decision Authority
214806a4 [grok-build-0.1] #   - Where should the logic live for "should this bot respond?"
214806a4 [grok-build-0.1] #     - In the central relay (centralized control)?
214806a4 [grok-build-0.1] #     - In each bot process (decentralized, each bot filters for itself)?
214806a4 [grok-build-0.1] #     - A mix (e.g. relay does coarse routing, bots do fine filtering)?
214806a5 [grok-build-0.1] #
214806a5 [grok-build-0.1] #4. Conversation Context
214806a5 [grok-build-0.1] #   - Should each bot maintain its own independent history/context?
214806a5 [grok-build-0.1] #   - Or should there be a shared session that all three bots can see?
214806a6 [grok-build-0.1] #   - Or something in between (shared project state, but per-bot conversation state)?
214806a6 [grok-build-0.1] #
214806a6 [grok-build-0.1] #5. Message Types
214806a6 [grok-build-0.1] #   - Are there different categories of messages that need different handling?
214806a7 [grok-build-0.1] #     - User messages directed at the system
214806a7 [grok-build-0.1] #     - System announcements
214806a7 [grok-build-0.1] #     - Tool results / internal events
214806a7 [grok-build-0.1] #     - Bot-to-bot communication
214806a7 [grok-build-0.1] #     - Commands
214806a7 [grok-build-0.1] #
214806a8 [grok-build-0.1] #6. Connection Model
214806a8 [grok-build-0.1] #   - One relay process managing multiple bot connections (current direction).
214806a8 [grok-build-0.1] #   - Should each bot still be a completely separate process, or could some be collapsed later?
214806a8 [grok-build-0.1] #   - How do you want to handle bot startup/shutdown and reconnection?
214806a9 [grok-build-0.1] #
214806a9 [grok-build-0.1] #Likely cause of "react in unison"
214806a9 [grok-build-0.1] #
214806a9 [grok-build-0.1] #From the shape of the current code, the most probable reasons are:
214806aa [grok-build-0.1] #- Broadcasts are sent to every connected client without routing metadata.
214806aa [grok-build-0.1] #- The bots don't have strong enough identity or filtering logic when they receive a message.
214806aa [grok-build-0.1] #- The main relay doesn't tag messages with an intended recipient.
214806aa [grok-build-0.1] #
214806ab [grok-build-0.1] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
214806ab [grok-build-0.1] #
214806ab [grok-build-0.1] #Before we go deeper, I’d like to understand your intent:
214806ab [grok-build-0.1] #
214806ac [grok-build-0.1] #- What is the desired behavior when a user posts a message in the Discord channel(s)?
214806ac [grok-build-0.1] #- Should the three bots have distinct personalities/roles, or are they mostly interchangeable right
214806ac [grok-build-0.1] #now?
214806ac [grok-build-0.1] #- Do you want users to be able to choose which bot they’re talking to, or should the system decide?
214806ad [grok-build-0.1] #- Is there any scenario where you want more than one bot to respond to the same message?
214806ad [grok-build-0.1] #
214806ad [grok-build-0.1] #Reply with your thoughts on any of the above (or add your own constraints), and we can sketch out a
214806ad [grok-build-0.1] #cleaner architecture.
214806ae [grok-build-0.1] #
