214811b5 [grok-build-0.1] #• Understood.* That's a clean and strong starting constraint.
214811b5 [grok-build-0.1] #
214811b6 [grok-build-0.1] #Starting rule: Bots only respond when @mentioned
214811b6 [grok-build-0.1] #
214811b6 [grok-build-0.1] #This is a good, simple foundation.
214811b6 [grok-build-0.1] #
214811b7 [grok-build-0.1] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
214811b7 [grok-build-0.1] #
214811b7 [grok-build-0.1] #Key implications of this rule
214811b7 [grok-build-0.1] #
214811b8 [grok-build-0.1] #This decision pushes us toward a few important architectural choices. Here are the main ones worth
214811b8 [grok-build-0.1] #deciding on early:
214811b8 [grok-build-0.1] #
214811b8 [grok-build-0.1] #1. Where does the @mention filtering happen?
214811b9 [grok-build-0.1] #
214811b9 [grok-build-0.1] #This is the biggest near-term decision.
214811b9 [grok-build-0.1] #
214811b9 [grok-build-0.1] #• Option A: In the bot (slopbot.ts)*
214811ba [grok-build-0.1] #- The Discord bot checks if it was mentioned.
214811ba [grok-build-0.1] #- If not mentioned → it ignores the message entirely (doesn't send it to the relay).
214811ba [grok-build-0.1] #- If mentioned → it forwards the message to the relay.
214811ba [grok-build-0.1] #
214811bb [grok-build-0.1] #• Option B: In the relay*
214811bb [grok-build-0.1] #- Every message still goes to the relay.
214811bb [grok-build-0.1] #- The relay decides which bot(s) should see it based on mentions, then routes accordingly.
214811bc [grok-build-0.1] #
214811bc [grok-build-0.1] #• My current lean:* Option A (in the bot) is probably better to start with. It reduces
214811bc [grok-build-0.1] #unnecessary traffic and keeps the filtering close to where the mention data already exists cleanly
214811bc [grok-build-0.1] #in Discord.
214811bd [grok-build-0.1] #
214811bd [grok-build-0.1] #Would you like to go with that direction for now?
214811bd [grok-build-0.1] #
214811bd [grok-build-0.1] #2. Commands (`/push`, `/model`, `/share`, etc.)
214811be [grok-build-0.1] #
214811be [grok-build-0.1] #Should commands require an @mention to work, or should they work without one?
214811be [grok-build-0.1] #
214811be [grok-build-0.1] #Examples:
214811bf [grok-build-0.1] #- Can someone type `/reset` on its own and have it affect the system?
214811bf [grok-build-0.1] #- Or must it be `@sloppy /reset`?
214811bf [grok-build-0.1] #
214811bf [grok-build-0.1] #This affects whether commands are treated as "bot-specific" or "system-wide".
214811c0 [grok-build-0.1] #
214811c0 [grok-build-0.1] #3. Non-mention messages
214811c0 [grok-build-0.1] #
214811c0 [grok-build-0.1] #What should happen to regular chat messages that don't @mention any bot?
214811c0 [grok-build-0.1] #
214811c1 [grok-build-0.1] #- Completely ignored (even by the relay)?
214811c1 [grok-build-0.1] #- Still logged / visible in the relay for history and context?
214811c1 [grok-build-0.1] #- Forwarded to the relay but not acted on by any bot?
214811c1 [grok-build-0.1] #
214811c2 [grok-build-0.1] #4. Bot Identity on Connection
214811c2 [grok-build-0.1] #
214811c2 [grok-build-0.1] #Even with @-only behavior, the relay will probably still need to know which bot is
214811c2 [grok-build-0.1] #connected on each TCP connection.
214811c3 [grok-build-0.1] #
214811c3 [grok-build-0.1] #Do you want the bots to announce their identity when they connect (e.g. "I am sloppy")?
214811c3 [grok-build-0.1] #
214811c3 [grok-build-0.1] #5. Multiple bots mentioned
214811c4 [grok-build-0.1] #
214811c4 [grok-build-0.1] #What should happen if someone @mentions two bots in one message?
214811c4 [grok-build-0.1] #
214811c4 [grok-build-0.1] #- Both respond?
214811c5 [grok-build-0.1] #- Only the first one?
214811c5 [grok-build-0.1] #- None (ambiguous)?
214811c5 [grok-build-0.1] #- Something else?
214811c5 [grok-build-0.1] #
214811c6 [grok-build-0.1] #6. System / Internal Messages
214811c6 [grok-build-0.1] #
214811c6 [grok-build-0.1] #Messages that come from the relay (tool results, status, announcements, etc.) will still
214811c6 [grok-build-0.1] #need to reach the bots.
214811c7 [grok-build-0.1] #
214811c7 [grok-build-0.1] #These should not require an @mention, correct? They need a separate path.
214811c7 [grok-build-0.1] #
