21482a61 [grok-build-0.1] # ꔀ Relay 1.9.1 grok-build-0.1 𝕏 🪠 0.7° $0.116 358.6KB 10.04s
21482a61 [grok-build-0.1] #• Got it.*
21482a62 [grok-build-0.1] #
21482a62 [grok-build-0.1] #Using a string array of names for mentions (`mentions: ["sloppy", "riff"]`) is a simple and
21482a62 [grok-build-0.1] #explicit approach. It keeps the tagging lightweight while still allowing the relay to express
21482a62 [grok-build-0.1] #intent clearly.
21482a63 [grok-build-0.1] #
21482a63 [grok-build-0.1] #How this could work conceptually
21482a63 [grok-build-0.1] #
21482a63 [grok-build-0.1] #- When the relay sends a message outward (via the current broadcast mechanism), it includes a
21482a64 [grok-build-0.1] #`mentions` array.
21482a64 [grok-build-0.1] #- Each bot receives the message and checks: "Is my name in the `mentions` array?"
21482a64 [grok-build-0.1] #  - If yes → process and emit to Discord.
21482a64 [grok-build-0.1] #  - If no → ignore.
21482a65 [grok-build-0.1] #- This gives the relay control over who should act, without the bots having to do complex
21482a65 [grok-build-0.1] #filtering.
21482a65 [grok-build-0.1] #
21482a65 [grok-build-0.1] #This fits well with the earlier decisions:
21482a66 [grok-build-0.1] #- Relay owns the long-lived state and can build the `mentions` array with full context.
21482a66 [grok-build-0.1] #- Bots stay relatively dumb about routing.
21482a66 [grok-build-0.1] #
21482a66 [grok-build-0.1] #Things this decision surfaces
21482a67 [grok-build-0.1] #
21482a67 [grok-build-0.1] #Here are the main areas we should clarify:
21482a67 [grok-build-0.1] #
21482a67 [grok-build-0.1] #1. Source of the array
21482a68 [grok-build-0.1] #   - The array would primarily come from parsing the original Discord @mentions in the incoming
21482a68 [grok-build-0.1] #message.
21482a68 [grok-build-0.1] #   - Should the relay ever add names to the array on its own (for example, for system
21482a68 [grok-build-0.1] #messages or when it wants to force a specific bot to speak)?
21482a69 [grok-build-0.1] #
21482a69 [grok-build-0.1] #2. Messages with no mentions
