214a46f9 [nitro@ryzen5] C:/nitrologic/entheogen/dip/dip.c:469:1: error: return type defaults to 'int' [-Wimplicit-int]  469 | sysini()
214a4780 [grok-build-0.1] # ꔀ Relay 1.9.1 grok-build-0.1 𝕏 🪣  0.7° $0.039 121.3KB 8.04s
214a4780 [grok-build-0.1] #The error is specifically about implicit int on the definition of `sysini()`.
214a4780 [grok-build-0.1] #
214a4780 [grok-build-0.1] #Why this error appears
214a4780 [grok-build-0.1] #Modern compilers (C99 and later, especially with `-Werror` or strict warning settings) no longer
214a4781 [grok-build-0.1] #allow a function definition to start without an explicit return type. When the compiler sees:
214a4781 [grok-build-0.1] #
214a4781 [grok-build-0.1] #
214a4781 [grok-build-0.1] #sysini()
214a4781 [grok-build-0.1] #
214a4782 [grok-build-0.1] #
214a4782 [grok-build-0.1] #it assumes the return type is `int` by default. This is the old pre-ANSI "implicit int" rule that
214a4782 [grok-build-0.1] #was removed from the language.
214a4783 [grok-build-0.1] #
214a4783 [grok-build-0.1] #Context in this file
214a4783 [grok-build-0.1] #- Earlier in the file there is already a forward declaration that correctly specifies `void
214a4783 [grok-build-0.1] #sysini();`
214a4784 [grok-build-0.1] #- The actual definition (around line 469) is written in pure K&R style without repeating the return
214a4784 [grok-build-0.1] #type.
214a4784 [grok-build-0.1] #- This creates a mismatch between the declaration and the definition that modern compilers now
214a4784 [grok-build-0.1] #reject.
214a4785 [grok-build-0.1] #
214a4785 [grok-build-0.1] #Nature of the function
214a4785 [grok-build-0.1] #`sysini()` performs setup work (opening the game file, determining memory, setting up the save
214a4785 [grok-build-0.1] #filename) and does not return any value. The call site in `main()` also treats it as a void
214a4785 [grok-build-0.1] #function.
214a4786 [grok-build-0.1] #
214a4786 [grok-build-0.1] #This is one of the first of many similar legacy patterns in this codebase, since it originates from
214a4786 [grok-build-0.1] #1986-era C.
214a4786 [grok-build-0.1] #
214a4787 [grok-build-0.1] #Would you like to discuss what to expect once this is resolved (i.e. the next likely error), or any
214a4787 [grok-build-0.1] #other aspect of this particular warning?
214a4787 [grok-build-0.1] #
