215d760d [grok-build-0.1] #
215d760d [grok-build-0.1] #Quick breakdown:
215d760e [grok-build-0.1] #
215d760e [grok-build-0.1] #• 1. `sloppy.bat`*
215d760e [grok-build-0.1] #Standard launcher stub. Just echoes a bit and runs `deno task sloppy`. Nothing special here.
215d760e [grok-build-0.1] #
215d760e [grok-build-0.1] #• 2. `dip.c`* (88669 bytes)
215d760f [grok-build-0.1] #This is a complete, self-contained Z-machine interpreter (ZIP-derived) from ~1986 with heavy
215d760f [grok-build-0.1] #graphics extensions for the AT&T UNIX PC / 7300 environment (TAM, windows, alternate screen buffer,
215d760f [grok-build-0.1] #icon/blockset handling).
215d760f [grok-build-0.1] #
215d760f [grok-build-0.1] #Key characteristics:
215d7610 [grok-build-0.1] #- Adapted from "Unix ZIP by Duncan Blanchard"
215d7610 [grok-build-0.1] #- Supports the usual 0/1/2/ext ops plus DIP-specific graphics ops (`OPSHOWI`, `OPSETI`, `OPSWAPI`,
215d7610 [grok-build-0.1] #`OPSHOWN`, `OPITER`, `OPWIND`, etc.)
215d7610 [grok-build-0.1] #- Custom paging/LRU system
215d7610 [grok-build-0.1] #- Preload + paged memory model
215d7611 [grok-build-0.1] #- Icon iteration tables, masking, clipping, alternate screen for faster graphics
215d7611 [grok-build-0.1] #- Save/restore, verify, random, etc. all present
215d7611 [grok-build-0.1] #- Lots of internal comments about the adaptation, EZIP notes, and platform-specific hacks (rev_byte
215d7611 [grok-build-0.1] #table for the AT&T display, etc.)
215d7611 [grok-build-0.1] #
215d7612 [grok-build-0.1] #On "original":
215d7612 [grok-build-0.1] #
215d7612 [grok-build-0.1] #It is not a from-scratch original implementation. The header and edit history explicitly
215d7612 [grok-build-0.1] #state it was adapted from an existing Unix ZIP. However, the graphics layer (blocksets, icons,
215d7612 [grok-build-0.1] #`op_showicon`/`iterate`/`md_drawblock`, alternate screen handling, `rev_byte`, etc.) appears to be
215d7612 [grok-build-0.1] #specific work for the DIP graphics system on that platform.
215d7613 [grok-build-0.1] #
215d7613 [grok-build-0.1] #This version is quite platform-specific (AT&T 7300 + TAM + `wind.h` + `urdata` raster ops). It is
215d7613 [grok-build-0.1] #not one of the more commonly circulated plain ZIP sources. I don't have an exact public match in my
215d7613 [grok-build-0.1] #training data for this precise combination of DIP graphics + AT&T TAM code, so in that narrow sense
215d7613 [grok-build-0.1] #the adaptation looks uncommon/rare.
215d7614 [grok-build-0.1] #
215d7614 [grok-build-0.1] #If you have a specific claim or question (e.g. "is this the original DIP interpreter source?" or
215d7614 [grok-build-0.1] #"does this match X other file?"), give me more context and I can dig into particular sections.
215d7614 [grok-build-0.1] #
215d7614 [grok-build-0.1] #What would you like to do with it?
215d7614 [grok-build-0.1] #- Comment on particular functions/areas
215d7615 [grok-build-0.1] #- Help extract or document the DIP graphics layer
215d7615 [grok-build-0.1] #- Look for modernization opportunities
215d7615 [grok-build-0.1] #- Something else
215d7615 [grok-build-0.1] #
215d7615 [grok-build-0.1] #Just say the word.
215d7616 [grok-build-0.1] #
