21746aa3 [glm-5.2] #
21746aa3 [glm-5.2] #• Bot message path:*
21746aa4 [glm-5.2] #
21746aa4 [glm-5.2] #1. A Discord bot (e.g. sloppy) sends a message to relay via TCP on port 8081
21746aa4 [glm-5.2] #2. `slopPrompt` receives it as `{messages:[{message:{content}, from:"sloppy"}]}`
21746aa4 [glm-5.2] #3. In the `chat()` loop, `m.from` is captured and logged for the incoming message via
21746aa5 [glm-5.2] #`logForge(content, m.from)` — so the bot's name does appear in the log for input
21746aa5 [glm-5.2] #4. The content is pushed to `lines` with `["sloppy"] ` prefixed
