2174c99b [glm-5.2] #
2174c99c [glm-5.2] #
2174c99c [glm-5.2] #The bot's own name (`sloppy`) is not in the payload. It's only known to the bot process
2174c99c [glm-5.2] #itself via `botName=Deno.args[1]`.
2174c99c [glm-5.2] #
2174c99d [glm-5.2] #In `relay.ts` `chat()`, `m.from` is `"skudmarks@discord"` — that gets logged for the input line via
2174c99d [glm-5.2] #`logForge(content, m.from)`. Good. But then `relay(0, from)` is called with `from=rohaUser` —
2174c99d [glm-5.2] #hardcoded, not `m.from`, and definitely not the bot name.
2174c99d [glm-5.2] #
2174c99e [glm-5.2] #• Outgoing (Relay → Discord):*
2174c99e [glm-5.2] #
2174c99e [glm-5.2] #In `relay()`, the reply is broadcast via `slopBroadcast("<4assistant>["+from+"]"+content, from)`.
2174c99e [glm-5.2] #Since `from` is `rohaUser`, the bot receives `from=rohaUser` and has no idea which bot should
2174c99f [glm-5.2] #respond.
2174c99f [glm-5.2] #
2174c99f [glm-5.2] #In `relaybot.ts` `onFountain()`, the filter is:
2174c99f [glm-5.2] #
2174c9a0 [glm-5.2] #if(from=="slop" && botName!="foggy") continue;
2174c9a0 [glm-5.2] #
2174c9a0 [glm-5.2] #So all bots receive all broadcasts, and only `from=="slop"` is filtered. Every bot posts every
2174c9a0 [glm-5.2] #reply.
2174c9a1 [glm-5.2] #
2174c9a1 [glm-5.2] #• The core problem:*
2174c9a1 [glm-5.2] #
2174c9a1 [glm-5.2] #The bot's persona name (`sloppy`, `riff`, `foggy`) never reaches relay. It exists only in
2174c9a2 [glm-5.2] #`relaybot.ts` as `botName` and `sloppyInfo[botName]`. The TCP payload carries the Discord user's
2174c9a2 [glm-5.2] #identity but not the bot's.
2174c9a2 [glm-5.2] #
2174c9a2 [glm-5.2] #• Options to fix:*
2174c9a2 [glm-5.2] #
2174c9a3 [glm-5.2] #1. Bot includes its name in the payload — e.g.
2174c9a3 [glm-5.2] #`{"messages":[{"message":"hello","from":"skudmarks@discord","bot":"sloppy"}]}`. Relay then threads
2174c9a3 [glm-5.2] #`bot` through to `relay()` as the persona tag for logging and broadcast routing.
2174c9a3 [glm-5.2] #
2174c9a4 [glm-5.2] #2. Relay tracks connections — map each TCP connection to a bot name. The bot could announce
2174c9a4 [glm-5.2] #itself on connect (it already sends `{"action":"connect"}` — could become
2174c9a4 [glm-5.2] #`{"action":"connect","bot":"sloppy"}`).
2174c9a5 [glm-5.2] #
2174c9a5 [glm-5.2] #3. Use `from` for the bot name — set `from` to `sloppy` in the payload instead of the
2174c9a5 [glm-5.2] #Discord user. But then you lose the Discord user's identity in the log, which seems worse.
2174c9a5 [glm-5.2] #
2174c9a5 [glm-5.2] #Option 1 seems cleanest — minimal change to the payload, the bot name flows naturally through the
2174c9a6 [glm-5.2] #existing `messages` array, and relay can use it for both logging and broadcast routing. The Discord
2174c9a6 [glm-5.2] #user's identity is still preserved in `from`.
2174c9a6 [glm-5.2] #
2174c9a6 [glm-5.2] #Which direction are you leaning?
2174c9a7 [glm-5.2] #
