21896b87 [glm-5.2] #load_elf32()          ← one breakpoint, one read, done
21896b87 [glm-5.2] #  → buf.data()        ← everything lives here
21896b88 [glm-5.2] #  → buf + e_phoff     ← cast to elf32_phdr*, inspect immediately
21896b88 [glm-5.2] #  → buf + e_shoff     ← cast to elf32_shdr*, inspect immediately
21896b88 [glm-5.2] #
21896b88 [glm-5.2] #
21896b89 [glm-5.2] #- One function to step into, one return value to inspect.
21896b89 [glm-5.2] #- In a debugger you can dump `content` and see the whole file.
21896b89 [glm-5.2] #- Pointer math is trivial — `content.data() + offset` evaluates instantly in a watch window.
21896b8a [glm-5.2] #- No repeated `ifstream` opens, seeks, or `gcount()` checks to step over.
