21896b8a [glm-5.2] #Seek-based (previous)
21896b8a [glm-5.2] #
21896b8b [glm-5.2] #load_elf32_header()   ← open, read, close
21896b8b [glm-5.2] #load_elf32_phdrs()    ← open, seek, read, close
21896b8b [glm-5.2] #load_elf32_shdrs()    ← open, seek, read, close
21896b8b [glm-5.2] #load_shstrtab()       ← open, seek, read, close
21896b8b [glm-5.2] #
21896b8c [glm-5.2] #
21896b8c [glm-5.2] #- Four functions, each with its own open/seek/read/error path.
21896b8c [glm-5.2] #- Each returns a separate vector — more variables to track.
21896b8c [glm-5.2] #- More code to step through for the same result.
21896b8d [glm-5.2] #
21896b8d [glm-5.2] #Your current `load_elf32` is the right call. The only thing needed is to bring `elf32_phdr` and
21896b8d [glm-5.2] #`elf32_shdr` back out of the comment block so the `ph`/`sh` pointers have something to cast to.
