218a7283 [glm-5.2] #I spotted two small things in this output that you might want to tweak:
218a7283 [glm-5.2] #
218a7284 [glm-5.2] #1. The Quotes are Misplaced
218a7284 [glm-5.2] #Look at the formatting of your section output:
218a7284 [glm-5.2] #`[ELF32] sh1:{name:".text, type:PROGBITS"}`
218a7284 [glm-5.2] #The closing quote `"` is at the very end of the string, capturing both the name and the type. You
218a7285 [glm-5.2] #probably want to move the `\"` in your `cout` statement to right after the name, like this:
218a7285 [glm-5.2] #
218a7285 [glm-5.2] #std::cout << "[ELF32] sh" << i << ":{name:\"" << (strtab + sh[i].sh_name)
218a7285 [glm-5.2] #          << "\", type:\"" << shtype_str << "\"}" << std::endl;
218a7286 [glm-5.2] #
218a7286 [glm-5.2] #So it outputs: `{name:".text", type:"PROGBITS"}`
218a7286 [glm-5.2] #
218a7286 [glm-5.2] #2. The ARM Types are Swapped (My Apologies!)
218a7287 [glm-5.2] #You might notice this oddity:
218a7287 [glm-5.2] #`sh3:{name:".ARM.exidx, type:ARM_ATTRIBUTES"}`
218a7287 [glm-5.2] #`sh25:{name:".ARM.attributes, type:ARM_EXIDX"}`
218a7288 [glm-5.2] #
218a7288 [glm-5.2] #This is actually my fault. In the `shtypes` map I gave you earlier, I accidentally swapped
218a7288 [glm-5.2] #the hex values for those two types!
218a7289 [glm-5.2] #• `0x70000001` is actually `ARM_EXIDX` (Exception Index).
218a7289 [glm-5.2] #• `0x70000003` is actually `ARM_ATTRIBUTES`.
218a7289 [glm-5.2] #
218a7289 [glm-5.2] #To fix it, just swap the strings in your `shtypes` map in `elf32.h`:
218a728a [glm-5.2] #
218a728a [glm-5.2] #{0x70000001, "ARM_EXIDX"},
218a728a [glm-5.2] #{0x70000003, "ARM_ATTRIBUTES"}
218a728b [glm-5.2] #
218a728b [glm-5.2] #
218a728b [glm-5.2] #Once you fix that quote placement and swap those strings, your section dump will be absolutely
218a728b [glm-5.2] #flawless.
218a728c [glm-5.2] #
218a728c [glm-5.2] #You've built a highly capable ELF inspector. What's the next move?
