218e0844 [glm-5.2] #char*` makes the loop much easier to read.
218e0844 [glm-5.2] #
218e0845 [glm-5.2] #Just a quick reminder: you have the forward declaration `void dumpMem(const uint8_t* values, int
218e0845 [glm-5.2] #base32, size_t size);` at the top of `elfutil.cpp`, but you still need to paste the actual
218e0845 [glm-5.2] #implementation of the function into the file (or into `elf32.h` if you prefer) to resolve the
218e0845 [glm-5.2] #linker error.
218e0845 [glm-5.2] #
218e0845 [glm-5.2] #Once that's in, you'll have a fully functional section dumper. Where would you like to go next? We
218e0846 [glm-5.2] #could:
218e0846 [glm-5.2] #1. Wire up `print_symbols` to see if `0x1000014d` resolves to a specific function name.
218e0846 [glm-5.2] #2. Make the section to dump configurable via `argv[2]` instead of hardcoding `.text`.
218e0846 [glm-5.2] #3. Add bounds checking to ensure `sh_offset + sh_size` doesn't exceed the file length.
