219dc8de [glm-5.2] #Thank you for sharing these files. I've reviewed all three and have a few observations:
219dc8de [glm-5.2] #
219dc8df [glm-5.2] #• elf32.h*
219dc8df [glm-5.2] #
219dc8df [glm-5.2] #The helper functions `typeString()` and `pflags_string()` are defined (not just declared) in the
219dc8df [glm-5.2] #header without `inline`. This will cause multiple-definition linker errors if the header is
219dc8df [glm-5.2] #included from more than one translation unit. Marking them `inline` or moving the definitions to a
219dc8df [glm-5.2] #`.cpp` would resolve this.
219dc8e0 [glm-5.2] #
219dc8e0 [glm-5.2] #• elfutil.cpp*
219dc8e0 [glm-5.2] #
219dc8e0 [glm-5.2] #A potential crash in the section header loop at line:
219dc8e0 [glm-5.2] #
219dc8e1 [glm-5.2] #
219dc8e1 [glm-5.2] #auto shtype = shtypes.find(sh[i].sh_type)->second;
219dc8e1 [glm-5.2] #
219dc8e1 [glm-5.2] #
219dc8e2 [glm-5.2] #If `sh[i].sh_type` is not in the `shtypes` map, `find()` returns `end()` and dereferencing it is
219dc8e2 [glm-5.2] #undefined behaviour. A safe pattern would be:
219dc8e2 [glm-5.2] #
219dc8e2 [glm-5.2] #
219dc8e2 [glm-5.2] #auto it = shtypes.find(sh[i].sh_type);
219dc8e3 [glm-5.2] #std::string shtype = (it != shtypes.end()) ? it->second : "UNKNOWN";
219dc8e3 [glm-5.2] #
219dc8e3 [glm-5.2] #
219dc8e4 [glm-5.2] #This mirrors the null-check already done in `emachine_string()` and `typeString()`.
219dc8e4 [glm-5.2] #
219dc8e4 [glm-5.2] #• relay.md*
219dc8e4 [glm-5.2] #
219dc8e5 [glm-5.2] #The transcript confirms the tool successfully parsed an ARM ELF32 executable with 8 program headers
219dc8e5 [glm-5.2] #and 32 sections. The documentation of `elf32_phdr` and `elf32_shdr` fields is accurate and serves
219dc8e5 [glm-5.2] #as useful inline reference.
219dc8e5 [glm-5.2] #
219dc8e6 [glm-5.2] #• General design note*
219dc8e6 [glm-5.2] #
219dc8e6 [glm-5.2] #The `content` vector stores everything after the ELF header, so every offset access
219dc8e6 [glm-5.2] #subtracts `sizeof(elf32)`. This works but is a recurring source of off-by-one errors. An
219dc8e7 [glm-5.2] #alternative would be to store the entire file in `content` and index from offset 0 directly,
219dc8e7 [glm-5.2] #eliminating the manual subtraction throughout.
219dc8e7 [glm-5.2] #
219dc8e8 [glm-5.2] #Everything else looks consistent between the header and implementation. Let me know if you'd like
219dc8e8 [glm-5.2] #me to elaborate on any of these points or assist with further development.
