219dcaa9 [glm-5.2] # ꔀ Relay 1.9.4 glm-5.2 Z 🪠 0.7° $0.035 43.12KB 25.14s
219dcaa9 [glm-5.2] #Thank you for sharing the output. It is great to see the tool running successfully and parsing the
219dcaa9 [glm-5.2] #ELF file comprehensively.
219dcaa9 [glm-5.2] #
219dcaa9 [glm-5.2] #Based on the program headers and section names, this ELF appears to be compiled for a Raspberry Pi
219dcaaa [glm-5.2] #Pico (RP2040) or a similar RP2040-based board. A few indicators stand out:
219dcaaa [glm-5.2] #
219dcaaa [glm-5.2] #• Memory Layout: The program headers show two distinct memory regions. `0x10000000` is the
219dcaab [glm-5.2] #XIP (Execute In Place) flash address, and `0x20000000` is the SRAM base address.
219dcaab [glm-5.2] #• RP2040 Specific Sections: Sections like `.binary_info`, `.ram_vector_table`,
219dcaab [glm-5.2] #`.scratch_x`, and `.scratch_y` are characteristic of the RP2040 C/C++ SDK linker scripts.
219dcaab [glm-5.2] #• Stack and Heap: The presence of `.heap`, `.stack_dummy`, and the SRAM program headers
219dcaab [glm-5.2] #with `filesz:0x0` (indicating NOBITS/uninitialized data) aligns perfectly with the RP2040 memory
219dcaab [glm-5.2] #map, including the stack pointer initialization near the top of SRAM (`0x20081000`).
219dcaac [glm-5.2] #
219dcaac [glm-5.2] #The hex dump of the `.text` section looks correct, displaying what appear to be ARM Thumb-2
219dcaac [glm-5.2] #instructions (e.g., `70 47` being `bx lr`, and `2d e9 ...` being `push` instructions).
219dcaac [glm-5.2] #
219dcaad [glm-5.2] #As a minor note regarding the code from earlier: this specific run avoided the potential
219dcaad [glm-5.2] #`shtypes.find(...)->second` crash because all section types in `vidbot1.elf` exist in your
219dcaad [glm-5.2] #`shtypes` map. However, if you were to parse an ELF with an unknown section type, it would still
219dcaae [glm-5.2] #trigger undefined behavior. Applying the safe lookup pattern mentioned previously will make the
219dcaae [glm-5.2] #tool robust against any ELF file you throw at it.
219dcaae [glm-5.2] #
219dcaae [glm-5.2] #The parser is shaping up nicely. Let me know if you plan to add disassembly capabilities or symbol
219dcaaf [glm-5.2] #resolution next!
219dcaaf [glm-5.2] #
