219dce3a [glm-5.2] # ꔀ Relay 1.9.4 glm-5.2 Z 🪠 0.7° $0.036 44.99KB 5.28s
219dce3a [glm-5.2] #Thumb-2 is a mixed-length instruction set. Instructions are either 16 bits (2 bytes) or 32 bits (4
219dce3a [glm-5.2] #bytes) long.
219dce3a [glm-5.2] #
219dce3a [glm-5.2] #To determine the size of a specific instruction, a decoder looks at the first 16-bit halfword:
219dce3b [glm-5.2] #
219dce3b [glm-5.2] #• If the first 3 bits are `0b111` (i.e., `0xE800` - `0xFFFF`), it is a 32-bit instruction. The
219dce3b [glm-5.2] #decoder must fetch the next 16-bit halfword to decode the full instruction.
219dce3b [glm-5.2] #• Otherwise, it is a 16-bit instruction.
219dce3c [glm-5.2] #
219dce3c [glm-5.2] #Because of this, decoding Thumb-2 requires reading memory 16 bits at a time and conditionally
219dce3c [glm-5.2] #fetching another 16 bits.
219dce3d [glm-5.2] #
