21a032a2 [kimi-k2.7-code] #
21a032a2 [kimi-k2.7-code] #
21a032a2 [kimi-k2.7-code] #Notes:
21a032a3 [kimi-k2.7-code] #
21a032a3 [kimi-k2.7-code] #• `crc32_buffer` is the public symbol you can look for in your ELF symbol table.
21a032a3 [kimi-k2.7-code] #• Keep it non-static and compile with `-O1` or `-O2` to get a realistic instruction mix while still
21a032a3 [kimi-k2.7-code] #retaining the function as a distinct symbol. At `-O3` the compiler may inline `crc32_update` into
21a032a4 [kimi-k2.7-code] #the loop, which is fine and still produces good Thumb-2 coverage.
21a032a4 [kimi-k2.7-code] #• If you want to force the function to exist as its own block at higher optimization levels,
21a032a4 [kimi-k2.7-code] #declare it with `__attribute__((noinline))` on GCC/Clang.
21a032a4 [kimi-k2.7-code] #
