21df75e4 [nitro@ryzen5] what is type:ARM_EXIDX
21df762a [gpt-5.3-codex] #`ARM_EXIDX` is the ARM exception index table section/segment (`.ARM.exidx`).
21df762b [gpt-5.3-codex] #
21df762b [gpt-5.3-codex] #In plain terms:
21df762b [gpt-5.3-codex] #- It stores compact unwind metadata for functions.
21df762b [gpt-5.3-codex] #- Used by exception unwinding / stack backtrace mechanisms (e.g., C++ exceptions, fault unwinding).
21df762c [gpt-5.3-codex] #- It’s part of ARM EABI conventions.
21df762c [gpt-5.3-codex] #
21df762c [gpt-5.3-codex] #So in your output, `type:ARM_EXIDX` means that entry contains unwind index data, not executable
21df762c [gpt-5.3-codex] #code.
21df762d [gpt-5.3-codex] #
