21df7a58 [gpt-5.3-codex] #- Added `headerString()` + fixed section type labeling in `elf32.h`
21df7a59 [gpt-5.3-codex] #- Added runtime toggles (`dumpSymbols`, `dumpHeaders`, `dumpSections`)
21df7a59 [gpt-5.3-codex] #- Added a pass that filters program headers by `flags==7` (RWX)
21df7a59 [gpt-5.3-codex] #
21df7a59 [gpt-5.3-codex] #For your request:
21df7a5a [gpt-5.3-codex] #
21df7a5a [gpt-5.3-codex] #- `flags == 7` means `R|W|X` in your `pflags_string`.
21df7a5a [gpt-5.3-codex] #- If you want `dumpMem` there, the right source pointer is from program header file offset
21df7a5a [gpt-5.3-codex] #(`p_offset`), not section offset.
21df7a5b [gpt-5.3-codex] #- Since `content` starts after ELF header, pointer base should be:
21df7a5b [gpt-5.3-codex] #	- `content.data() + (ph[i].p_offset - sizeof(elf32))`
