21e74a87 [gemini-3.5-flash] # ꔀ Relay 1.9.4 gemini-3.5-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.021 9.886KB 9.92s
21e74a87 [gemini-3.5-flash] #In the Unicode Mathematical Operators block, the square subset and superset signs are
21e74a87 [gemini-3.5-flash] #surrounded by several closely related variations. These adjacent characters can be incredibly
21e74a87 [gemini-3.5-flash] #useful for representing special maze features—such as doors, one-way gates, keys, or start/end
21e74a87 [gemini-3.5-flash] #points.
21e74a88 [gemini-3.5-flash] #
21e74a88 [gemini-3.5-flash] #Here are the characters immediately adjacent to `⊏` and `⊐` in the Unicode table, along with other
21e74a88 [gemini-3.5-flash] #closely related families:
21e74a88 [gemini-3.5-flash] #
21e74a89 [gemini-3.5-flash] #1. The "Equal To" Variants (With Bottom Bars)
21e74a89 [gemini-3.5-flash] #These characters add a horizontal bar at the bottom, which visually resembles a U-shape with a
21e74a89 [gemini-3.5-flash] #shelf or a closed threshold.
21e74a89 [gemini-3.5-flash] #• `⊑` (Square Subset or Equal To) — `U+2291` (Open Right with bottom bar)
21e74a8a [gemini-3.5-flash] #• `⊒` (Square Superset or Equal To) — `U+2292` (Open Left with bottom bar)
21e74a8a [gemini-3.5-flash] #
21e74a8a [gemini-3.5-flash] #2. Negated Variants (With Slash-Throughs)
21e74a8a [gemini-3.5-flash] #If you need to represent a locked door, a blocked path, or a wall that cannot be passed, these
21e74a8b [gemini-3.5-flash] #negated versions of the square subset/superset signs fit the aesthetic perfectly:
21e74a8b [gemini-3.5-flash] #• `⋢` (Not Square Subset or Equal To) — `U+22E2`
21e74a8b [gemini-3.5-flash] #• `⋣` (Not Square Superset or Equal To) — `U+22E3`
21e74a8b [gemini-3.5-flash] #
21e74a8c [gemini-3.5-flash] #3. The Rounded Equivalents
21e74a8c [gemini-3.5-flash] #If you prefer a softer, rounded aesthetic for your maze paths, the standard set theory symbols
21e74a8c [gemini-3.5-flash] #provide the exact same four orientations in a curved style:
21e74a8c [gemini-3.5-flash] #• `∪` (Union / Open Top) — `U+222A`
21e74a8d [gemini-3.5-flash] #• `∩` (Intersection / Open Bottom) — `U+2229`
21e74a8d [gemini-3.5-flash] #• `⊂` (Subset / Open Right) — `U+2282`
21e74a8d [gemini-3.5-flash] #• `⊃` (Superset / Open Left) — `U+2283`
21e74a8d [gemini-3.5-flash] #
21e74a8e [gemini-3.5-flash] #4. Rounded Variants with Bars
21e74a8e [gemini-3.5-flash] #Just like the square versions, the rounded versions have "equal to" variants with bottom lines:
21e74a8e [gemini-3.5-flash] #• `⊆` (Subset or Equal To / Open Right with bar) — `U+2286`
21e74a8e [gemini-3.5-flash] #• `⊇` (Superset or Equal To / Open Left with bar) — `U+2287`
21e74a8f [gemini-3.5-flash] #• `⊈` (Not Subset or Equal To) — `U+2288`
21e74a8f [gemini-3.5-flash] #• `⊉` (Not Superset or Equal To) — `U+2289`
21e74a8f [gemini-3.5-flash] #
