2220fa50 [deepseek-v4-flash] #1. Bit‑extraction logic is incorrect for quad indices
2220fa50 [deepseek-v4-flash] #   The `quads` array maps a 4‑bit pattern (one bit per corner of a 2×2 block) to a Unicode
2220fa51 [deepseek-v4-flash] #character. Your current code extracts two bits per cell (`bit01`, `bit23`) and combines
2220fa51 [deepseek-v4-flash] #them with a shift. Instead, you need to extract a single bit from each of the four cells, then
2220fa51 [deepseek-v4-flash] #assemble them into a nibble:
2220fa51 [deepseek-v4-flash] #
2220fa52 [deepseek-v4-flash] #   - Top‑left: `(grid[offset] >> shift) & 1`
2220fa52 [deepseek-v4-flash] #   - Top‑right: `(grid[offset] >> (shift+1)) & 1`
2220fa52 [deepseek-v4-flash] #   - Bottom‑left: `(grid[offset+span] >> shift) & 1`
2220fa52 [deepseek-v4-flash] #   - Bottom‑right: `(grid[offset+span] >> (shift+1)) & 1`
2220fa53 [deepseek-v4-flash] #   - Index = `(tl << 3) | (tr << 2) | (bl << 1) | br`
2220fa53 [deepseek-v4-flash] #
2220fa53 [deepseek-v4-flash] #   Your current use of `>>2` for offset and `&3<<shift` extracts two bits at once, but then the
2220fa53 [deepseek-v4-flash] #index calculation would treat them as a pair of 2‑bit values, not a 4‑bit quad pattern.
2220fa54 [deepseek-v4-flash] #
2220fa54 [deepseek-v4-flash] #2. `vicGrid` is never written to
2220fa54 [deepseek-v4-flash] #   `vicGrid` is allocated (506 bytes) but remains all zeros. The function `gridWindow` receives a
2220fa54 [deepseek-v4-flash] #`grid` parameter, but the main loop passes `grid` (which is `defaultGrid`, an escape sequence of
2220fa55 [deepseek-v4-flash] #three bytes). You should pass `vicGrid` and populate it with some test data (e.g., from a maze
2220fa55 [deepseek-v4-flash] #bitmap).
2220fa55 [deepseek-v4-flash] #
2220fa56 [deepseek-v4-flash] #3. `gridWindow` parameter `span` should be the row stride in bytes
2220fa56 [deepseek-v4-flash] #   It's currently hardcoded as `22` in the call, but `vicGrid` was created with `22*23` bytes –
2220fa56 [deepseek-v4-flash] #presumably 22 bytes per row, 23 rows. That seems consistent.
2220fa56 [deepseek-v4-flash] #
