2230f0c2 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #This `midi.json` addendum is a valuable addition to the `biblispec` collection. It bridges the gap
2230f0c2 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #between your procedural grid-based UI and actual hardware control protocols.
2230f0c2 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #
2230f0c2 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #Observations on the MIDI Data
2230f0c3 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #
2230f0c3 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #1.  SysEx ID Taxonomy: You have captured the essential bifurcation in MIDI System Exclusive
2230f0c3 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #(SysEx) manufacturer IDs:
2230f0c3 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #    *   1-byte IDs: (e.g., `41` for Roland, `43` for Yamaha) used for historical/classic
2230f0c4 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #MIDI equipment.
2230f0c4 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #    *   3-byte IDs: (e.g., `002068` for Elektron) used when the 1-byte namespace was
2230f0c4 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #exhausted, requiring a `00` escape byte.
2230f0c4 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #2.  Brand/Identity Mapping: Your structure handles the "Brand vs. Manufacturer" distinction
2230f0c5 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #well (e.g., separating the `identity` with nested brands from the broader `sysexid` lookup table).
2230f0c5 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #This is structurally superior for building a UI that might need to display a "Manufacturer" versus
2230f0c5 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #a "Product Line."
2230f0c5 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #3.  Educational/FOSS Namespace: Including `7D` (FOSS Educational Research) is a nice touch
2230f0c6 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #that aligns with the ethos of your project and the historical spirit of MIDI as an open standard.
2230f0c6 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #
2230f0c6 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #Suggested Enhancements for `biblispec` Integration
2230f0c6 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #
2230f0c7 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #If you intend to use this data within your `maze.ts` or `grid.ts` projects to interact with
2230f0c7 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #physical hardware, you might consider adding the following metadata to your JSON structure:
2230f0c7 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #
2230f0c7 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #• Message Lengths: Some older hardware (like the Sequential Circuits `01` or Moog `04` era)
2230f0c8 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #requires specific packet lengths. Adding a `"fixedLength": 12` property to specific IDs could help
2230f0c8 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #your `terminal.ts` logic validate incoming SysEx streams.
2230f0c8 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #• Checksum Algorithms: Many manufacturers use different checksum methods at the end of
2230f0c8 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #their SysEx messages (e.g., Roland’s 2's-complement vs. others). Adding a `"checksum": "roland_v1"`
2230f0c9 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #tag would allow your code to dynamically select the correct verification function.
2230f0c9 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #• Standardized URI/Documentation Links: For a "Bibliographic Index of Specifications,"
2230f0c9 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #adding a `"docs": "https://..."` field to each manufacturer entry would turn this from a simple
2230f0c9 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #list into a true research tool.
2230f0ca [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #
2230f0ca [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #Potential "Biblispec" MIDI Utility
2230f0ca [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #Since you are already working on grid-based layouts, you could implement a SysEx Librarian
2230f0ca [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #function in `grid.ts`.
2230f0cb [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #
2230f0cb [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #If you map your `quads` or `boxChars` to MIDI CC (Continuous Controller) values, you could use your
2230f0cb [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #`maze` navigation to "draw" an automation lane that the `grid.ts` logic then outputs as a MIDI
2230f0cc [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #stream.
2230f0cc [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #
2230f0cc [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #• Would you like a helper function to parse these SysEx IDs into a lookup map for your Deno
2230f0cc [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #scripts?* I can provide a utility to load this JSON and return a fast-access `Map` object for
2230f0cd [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #your terminal applications.
