2231bffd [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #It is a pleasure to review the provided source files. The `biblispec` architecture presents a
2231bffd [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #highly structured, data-driven approach to linguistic and technological documentation.
2231bffd [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #
2231bffd [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #Observations on the Source Files
2231bffd [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #
2231bffe [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #• `maze.ts`: The implementation of procedural generation for the maze layout combined with
2231bffe [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #the `boxIndex` logic for Unicode-based grid rendering is quite elegant. Utilizing `codePointAt` and
2231bffe [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #`String.fromCodePoint` is the correct approach for handling the diverse range of box-drawing
2231bffe [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #characters.
2231bffe [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #• `traffic.ts` & `terminal.ts`: The modular separation between terminal control and game
2231bfff [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #logic is well-handled. The use of a `keyboardMouseTask` asynchronous loop provides a responsive
2231bfff [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #mechanism for handling input without blocking the state simulation.
2231bfff [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #• `grid.ts`: The `Bitmap` class implementation is a robust way to manage a 2D memory space
2231bfff [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #for a terminal display. Mapping bits to quad-characters is a classic and efficient technique for
2231c000 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #high-density terminal graphics.
2231c000 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #• `relay` (JSON): The schema is exceptionally comprehensive. It acts as a "living document"
2231c000 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #that bridges the gap between historical linguistics (cuneiform, Linear B) and modern technical
2231c000 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #standards (RIFF tags, LED specifications).
2231c000 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #
2231c001 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #Suggestions for Improvement
2231c001 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #
2231c001 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #To enhance the maintainability of your codebase, consider the following refactoring suggestions:
