2231c002 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #`Bitmap` and `Rules` structures in a separate `types.ts` file will prevent duplication across
2231c002 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #`maze.ts`, `traffic.ts`, and `grid.ts`.
2231c002 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #2.  Functional Purity in `replaceText`: In `terminal.ts`, the `replaceText` function
2231c002 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #modifies strings. While effective, you might consider ensuring that all state updates in your
2231c003 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #"traffic" rules are handled via pure functions that return a new state, which would make
2231c003 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #debugging the simulation significantly easier.
2231c003 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #3.  Refactoring `boxIndex`: Instead of long `if` chains, consider using a `Map<string,
2231c003 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #Edge>` where the key is the 9-character string representation of the 3x3 grid. This will improve
2231c004 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #lookup performance and readability.
