2232955d [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #Yes, you can import classes in Deno using standard TypeScript/JavaScript `import` statements. Deno
2232955d [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #treats files as modules, so as long as you export the class from the source file, it will be
2232955e [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #available for use in other files.
2232955e [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #
2232955e [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #Here is an example of how to structure this:
2232955e [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #
2232955f [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #1. The Class File (`User.ts`)
2232955f [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #Use the `export` keyword before the `class` declaration.
