2232d3a4 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #Pro-Tip for Deno
2232d3a4 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #When using these in production, ensure your program handles the `SIGINT` (Ctrl+C) signal. If your
2232d3a4 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #program exits while the cursor is hidden, the user's terminal will remain without a cursor until
2232d3a4 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #they restart it. You can use `Deno.addSignalListener("SIGINT", () => { showCursor(); Deno.exit();
2232d3a5 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] #});` to ensure the cursor is restored on exit.
